The threads table has been created with: UUID primary key (gen_random_uuid), user_id FK to auth.users with CASCADE delete, title with default 'New Chat', timestamps. Indexes: idx_threads_user_id and idx_threads_updated_at (DESC). The messages table has been created with: UUID primary key, thread_id FK to threads with CASCADE, user_id FK to auth.users with CASCADE, role CHECK constraint ('user', 'assistant', 'system'), content TEXT (defaulting to ''), tool_calls JSONB defaulting to empty array. Indexes: idx_messages_thread_id and idx_messages_created_at. Run migration with `npx supabase db reset` and verify tables exist.

Verification SQL:
```sql
-- Verify threads table structure
SELECT column_name, data_type, is_nullable, column_default FROM information_schema.columns WHERE table_name = 'threads' ORDER BY ordinal_position;
-- Verify messages table structure
SELECT column_name, data_type, is_nullable, column_default FROM information_schema.columns WHERE table_name = 'messages' ORDER BY ordinal_position;
-- Verify indexes exist
SELECT indexname FROM pg_indexes WHERE tablename IN ('threads', 'messages');
-- Verify foreign key constraints
SELECT tc.constraint_name, kcu.column_name, ccu.table_name AS foreign_table_name FROM information_schema.table_constraints AS tc JOIN information_schema.key_column_usage AS kcu ON tc.constraint_name = kcu.constraint_name JOIN information_schema.constraint_column_usage AS ccu ON ccu.constraint_name = tc.constraint_name WHERE tc.constraint_type = 'FOREIGN KEY' AND tc.table_name IN ('threads', 'messages');
```

The skills table has been created with: UUID primary key, nullable user_id FK (NULL = global skill), name VARCHAR(64) with regex validation (^[a-z][a-z0-9]*(-[a-z0-9]+)*$), description VARCHAR(1024) with min 20 char check, instructions TEXT, enabled boolean, license/compatibility VARCHAR(64), metadata JSONB. The unique index uses COALESCE to handle NULL user_id: COALESCE(user_id, '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000'::UUID). The skill_files table stores: skill_id FK, user_id FK, filename, file_size BIGINT, mime_type, storage_path. Index on skill_id.

Verification SQL:
```sql
-- Verify skills table structure
SELECT column_name, data_type, is_nullable, character_maximum_length FROM information_schema.columns WHERE table_name = 'skills' ORDER BY ordinal_position;
-- Verify check constraints
SELECT conname, pg_get_constraintdef(oid) FROM pg_constraint WHERE conrelid = 'skills'::regclass AND contype = 'c';
-- Verify unique index
SELECT indexname, indexdef FROM pg_indexes WHERE tablename = 'skills';
-- Test name validation
INSERT INTO skills (user_id, name, description, instructions) VALUES (NULL, 'test-skill', 'This is a valid skill description with at least 20 characters', 'Instructions here');
INSERT INTO skills (user_id, name, description, instructions) VALUES (NULL, 'INVALID', 'This should fail', 'test'); -- Should fail
```

The code_executions table has been created with: UUID primary key, thread_id FK to threads with CASCADE, user_id FK to auth.users with CASCADE, code TEXT, stdout/stderr TEXT nullable, exit_code INTEGER nullable, status CHECK ('running', 'completed', 'failed') defaulting to 'running', execution_time_ms INTEGER nullable, created_at timestamp. Index on thread_id. The sandbox_files table stores: UUID primary key, execution_id FK to code_executions with CASCADE, user_id FK, filename TEXT, file_size BIGINT, mime_type TEXT, storage_path TEXT, created_at timestamp. Index on execution_id.

Verification SQL:
```sql
-- Verify code_executions table structure
SELECT column_name, data_type, is_nullable, column_default FROM information_schema.columns WHERE table_name = 'code_executions' ORDER BY ordinal_position;
-- Verify sandbox_files table structure
SELECT column_name, data_type, is_nullable FROM information_schema.columns WHERE table_name = 'sandbox_files' ORDER BY ordinal_position;
-- Verify status check constraint
SELECT conname, pg_get_constraintdef(oid) FROM pg_constraint WHERE conrelid = 'code_executions'::regclass AND contype = 'c';
-- Verify indexes
SELECT indexname FROM pg_indexes WHERE tablename IN ('code_executions', 'sandbox_files');
```

RLS has been implemented for all 6 tables. Threads: users can only CRUD their own threads (auth.uid() = user_id). Messages: same ownership-based policies. Skills: SELECT allows viewing own skills OR global skills (user_id IS NULL), INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE restricted to own skills only. Skill_files: ownership-based policies, no UPDATE policy (files are immutable). Code_executions: ownership-based SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE, no DELETE policy. Sandbox_files: ownership-based SELECT/INSERT only.

Verification SQL:
```sql
-- Verify RLS is enabled on all tables
SELECT tablename, rowsecurity FROM pg_tables WHERE schemaname = 'public' AND tablename IN ('threads', 'messages', 'skills', 'skill_files', 'code_executions', 'sandbox_files');
-- List all RLS policies
SELECT tablename, policyname, cmd, qual, with_check FROM pg_policies WHERE schemaname = 'public' ORDER BY tablename, cmd;
-- Test global skills visibility (requires authenticated test user)
-- INSERT INTO skills (user_id, name, description, instructions) VALUES (NULL, 'global-test', 'A global skill visible to all users with proper description', 'test');
```

The updated_at trigger function has been created and applied to threads and skills tables. It automatically sets updated_at = NOW() on any UPDATE. Storage buckets created: 'skill-files' (private), 'sandbox-outputs' (private). Storage RLS policies enforce user path segregation using storage.foldername(name)[1] = auth.uid()::text pattern. This means files must be stored under /{user_id}/... path structure. Policies cover INSERT, SELECT, DELETE for skill-files and INSERT, SELECT for sandbox-outputs.

Verification SQL:
```sql
-- Verify trigger function exists
SELECT proname, prosrc FROM pg_proc WHERE proname = 'update_updated_at_column';
-- Verify triggers on tables
SELECT tgname, tgrelid::regclass FROM pg_trigger WHERE tgname LIKE 'update_%_updated_at';
-- Verify storage buckets exist
SELECT id, name, public FROM storage.buckets WHERE id IN ('skill-files', 'sandbox-outputs');
-- Verify storage policies
SELECT policyname, cmd FROM pg_policies WHERE tablename = 'objects' AND schemaname = 'storage';
-- Test trigger by updating a thread
-- UPDATE threads SET title = 'Updated Title' WHERE id = '...';
-- SELECT updated_at FROM threads WHERE id = '...'; -- Should show current timestamp
```

